PlantGuard Studio: three-minute classroom demonstration

Before class
Extract the entire ZIP. Python 3 and a current Chrome/Edge browser must already be installed. Open Start_PlantGuard.command on Mac or Start_PlantGuard.bat on Windows. Alternatively run python3 start.py in the extracted folder. Keep the terminal open. Test with Wi-Fi off.

1. Device studio (45 seconds)
Click Camera Module 3, then Raspberry Pi 4. Explain the CSI ribbon, local models and display. Say clearly: this is a hardware simulation running on our computer.

2. Unsuitable photo (45 seconds)
Open AI leaf scan and upload a laptop photograph. Run identification. A rejected or unclear input should receive no plant or disease name. The semantic screening model can still make mistakes; do not claim perfect rejection.

3. Leaf scan (45 seconds)
Upload a clear real leaf photograph. Run identification and explain the plant candidate, disease coverage and uncertainty. A leaf can pass screening while the plant identity remains uncertain. Save an observation only after reviewing it.

