neghani/plantvillage-mobilenetv2, Apache 2.0.
Source: https://huggingface.co/neghani/plantvillage-mobilenetv2/tree/d33601185b32cf05b3942661b8d84ffb86dc48ec
Original model.safetensors SHA256 f1a98e77629c36b5fe90a0fbed7ba56f097ce419c6dad8456bd135f36ea8d426
Converted by this project to ONNX opset 17, fixed 1x3x224x224 float32 input, unchanged weights. PyTorch / ONNX Runtime output maximum absolute difference 0.00001145 on a deterministic tensor. This checks conversion, not classification accuracy.
Resize short side 256, centre crop 224, scale RGB to [-1,1], NCHW. Browser canvas resize approximates Pillow bilinear filters. Softmax on 38 logits; no temperature calibration applied. Scores are uncalibrated model outputs.
38 crop-condition labels across 14 crop categories. Some labels are pests or healthy-labelled leaves, not diseases. Blueberry, raspberry and soybean have only healthy labels. Orange and squash have no healthy baseline. No model covers all diseases.
Author reports 99.17% held-out PlantVillage accuracy, but 16% top-1 on a small 25-image real-world set. Lab and field results differ sharply. Those author-reported values do not validate this application's preprocessing or local field performance. See bundled original model card.
Score >=0.70, margin >=0.20 and agreement with a confidently identified species are required for an accepted combined candidate. Unsupported species, weak identity and crop disagreement are flagged. This is not a reliable open-set detector. Non-plants and unseen species can still yield confident errors.

